      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not provide an explicit definition of “synergistic muscles” (e.g., that they are muscles within the same muscle group that act together to produce force or movement).",
        "The packet mentions “synergistic action of other muscle groups” and “synergistic muscles of the triceps brachii,” but it does not state the requested definitional relationship (within the same muscle group, acting together to produce force/movement).",
        "The second sentence (“even muscles working together… can differ in how they are activated as force or joint angle changes”) is broadly consistent with the packet’s discussion of differences in EMG activation patterns and RMS-force relationship changes, but since the core definition is unsupported, the definition as a whole is not defensible."
